---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout class="resume">
  <hgroup>
    <h1>Carter McBride</h1>
    <p>Software Engineer · Saratoga Springs, Utah</p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:jobs@carter.works">jobs@carter.works</a> ·
      <a href="https://carter.works">carter.works</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/carterworks">github.com/carterworks</a> ·
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thatcartermcbride/"
        >linkedin.com/in/thatcartermcbride</a
      >
    </p>
  </hgroup>

  <p>
    Web developer with eight years of professional experience, building small,
    fast JavaScript that runs on some of the world’s busiest websites. Happiest
    making builds simpler, bundles smaller and tests trustworthy.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Experience</h2>

    <article>
      <h3>Software Engineer, Adobe <span>Jan 2022 – Present</span></h3>
      <p>Lehi, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Develop the open-source Adobe Experience Platform Web SDK (<a
            href="https://github.com/adobe/alloy">adobe/alloy</a
          >), the data collection and personalization library on many of the
          world’s largest websites and storefronts, and its Adobe Tags
          extension: 250+ merged pull requests.
        </li>
        <li>
          Built datastream configuration overrides, which let customers change
          a datastream’s settings per page or per command, across the SDK and
          the extension’s UI.
        </li>
        <li>
          Dropped Internet Explorer support to cut the gzipped SDK by 9%, and
          added bundle-size reporting and browser-compatibility linting to
          every build.
        </li>
        <li>
          Merged the SDK and its extension into one pnpm monorepo, automated
          releases to npm and the CDN with Changesets, and moved the functional
          tests from TestCafe to Vitest, Playwright and Mock Service Worker.
        </li>
        <li>Developed the Adobe Experience Platform Debugger.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>
        Software Developer, ICE Mortgage Technology <span
          >Jan 2019 – Jan 2022</span
        >
      </h3>
      <p>Provo, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Improved performance on critical-path user features, and championed
          new, intuitive workflows for large customers.
        </li>
        <li>
          Mentored new employees and coached them on every part of software
          development; kept the software reliable with high test coverage.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Software Engineer, Lingotek <span>May 2018 – Dec 2018</span></h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Moved several pages of the main product to Vue.js, cutting page load
          times by 15%.
        </li>
        <li>
          Reworked a large project’s build, cutting build times by 25% and
          opening it to modern tools.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>
        Front-End Web Developer, Brigham Young University <span
          >Feb 2016 – May 2018</span
        >
      </h3>
      <p>Provo, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Built features for Learning Suite, BYU’s learning management system,
          used by thousands of students and faculty.
        </li>
        <li>
          Guarded data integrity with thorough unit tests, and automated setup
          for quick onboarding.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>
        Product Solutions Intern, Nu Skin Enterprises <span
          >May 2017 – Aug 2017</span
        >
      </h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Integrated company data with SharePoint and Azure Active Directory,
          working directly with internal customers.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://yazzy.carter.works">Yazzy</a>: reader mode for any
        website, in Astro.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/carterworks/substack-to-epub"
          >substack-to-epub</a
        >: saves a Substack newsletter to SQLite and binds it as an EPUB, in
        Python.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://carter.works">carter.works</a>: this site, with a
        pixel-art backdrop published as a reusable web components package.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://tools.carter.works">tools.carter.works</a>: a
        collection of single-file HTML tools.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <h3>
      B.S. Computer Science, Brigham Young University <span>2015 – 2019</span>
    </h3>
    <p>
      Minor in Portuguese. Association for Computing Machinery. Third place,
      BYU Google Games 2017.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Languages</dt>
      <dd>TypeScript, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Python, Go</dd>
      <dt>Web</dt>
      <dd>Web components, Astro, React, Vue.js, Node.js</dd>
      <dt>Tooling</dt>
      <dd>
        Vite, Rollup, Vitest, Playwright, pnpm, GitHub Actions, Claude Code
      </dd>
      <dt>Spoken</dt>
      <dd>English, Brazilian Portuguese</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(.resume) {
    --flow-space: var(--size-sm);

    display: grid;
    gap: var(--size-md);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 1.6em;
  }

  h2 {
    border-block-end: 1px solid;
    font-size: 1em;
    margin-block-end: var(--size-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h3 {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 1em;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  h3 span {
    font-weight: normal;
  }

  article + article {
    margin-block-start: var(--size-sm);
  }

  ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.2em;
  }

  dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0 var(--size-sm);
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  @media print {
    @page {
      margin: 0.5in;
      size: letter;
    }

    :global(html) {
      color-scheme: light;
      font-size: 10pt;
    }

    :global(body) {
      background: none;
      color: #000;
      display: block;
    }

    :global(pixel-backdrop),
    :global(body > .stack > header) {
      display: none;
    }

    :global(.resume) {
      background: none;
      gap: var(--size-sm);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    a {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    a[href]::after {
      content: none;
    }
  }
</style>
